    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section details the assessment of media consumption among participants, including hours spent watching television, looking at magazines, and using the Internet. Participants indicated their consumption on a scale from 0 to 6+ hours, with item scores averaged for each media form.",
      "evidence_source": "2.2.9. Media consumption In line with previous research (e.g., Hatoum &amp; Belle, 2004; Slater &amp; Tiggemann, 2006), participants indicated the number of hours spent, on average, (a) watching television each day; (b) looking at magazines each month; (c) using the Internet during the week; and (d) using the Internet on weekends, from 1 = 0 h to 8 = 6+ hours. Question (b) was assessed by type (fashion, health/fitness, sports, men's interest, gay). Item scores were averaged for each form of media separately; higher scores reflect higher levels of consumption of television, magazines, and Internet, respectively.",
